 "note": "International Trading Company Store (former), 83 Bussell Hwy, Margaret River's third store (1925), later the Margaret River Art Gallery and Jahroc, REDSEA Gallery since 2024 (local heritage list MR(T)-04). Placed from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), OSM (the old 'Jahroc Gallery' point) and 2019 street photos showing the Jah Roc signs: the complex just north of Wino's and south of the tyre shop's car park. A single-storey timber weatherboard shop, dark oiled timber, gabled to the street, with a lower gabled wing on its north side, a modern bull-nosed verandah over the footpath and a central entry between big timber-framed shop windows; behind it the 2005 flat-roofed contemporary gallery (black, deep red fascia), and the old cottage behind that (outbuilding). Name in plain lettering. Metres: x left to right as seen from Bussell Hwy (north to south), y back (east) from the shopfront. Outlines are the roofs in the aerial.",
